      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "MASt3R — Folder Input + Precision Tuning + Solidify + WASD Viewer\n\nPIPELINE:\n  Folder Input → Reconstruction → Mesh Filter → Solidify → 3D Viewer\n\nSTEP 1 — Pick your folder (left).\nSTEP 2 — Queue Prompt.\nSTEP 3 — Use the viewer (right): orbit, WASD, fullscreen, grid toggle, brightness, etc.\n\nWHAT EACH NODE TUNES:\n  • MASt3R 3D Reconstruction — niter=700, min_conf_thr=2.0, matching_conf_thr=1.0, TSDF_thresh=0.15 are all dialled up for precision over speed.\n  • Mesh Filter — passthrough by default; switch smoothing to 'taubin' iters 2-3 if surface is noisy.\n  • Solidify (NEW) — turns the patchy surface into a filled mesh:\n      voxel_close (default): voxelize + dilation + closing → fills small/medium gaps.\n      voxel_fill: only thicken; keeps holes intact.\n      convex_hull: shrink-wraps whole scene (use only for simple convex objects).\n      passthrough: skip solidify, use raw MASt3R output.\n  • voxel_resolution = 220 is a good balance (8GB RAM safe).  Bump to 350-400 for fine detail (slow).\n  • dilation/closing — raise both to fill bigger gaps.\n\nVRAM (8GB / RTX 4070):\n  • complete @ 512 for 6-12 images: comfortable.\n  • If OOM: drop image_size to 448 or switch scenegraph_type to swin."
      ]
    },
